## 💎 Key Attributes and Methods Specifications
BaseModel (Parent Class)
Provides identity and audit tracking across the entire architecture. All entities inherit from this base class to ensure consistency and simplify data management.

id (string): Unique identifier generated via secure UUID4.

created_at / updated_at (datetime): Automatic system timestamps capturing object history.

save(): Updates the updated_at field and flags the instance as ready to sync.

to_dict(): Serializes model attributes into a standard Python dictionary layout.

User
Defines any physical individual registered within the system ecosystem who can host properties or post feedback.

Attributes: first_name, last_name, email (Unique key), password (Hashed), is_admin (Role flag).

Methods: register() to enforce initialization constraints.

Place
The rental property unit offered by hosts on the platform.

Attributes: title, description, price (Enforced positive float), address, max_guests, owner_id (Foreign link to User).

Review
Feedback and textual commentary submitted by a guest evaluating a specific rental property.

Attributes: comment, rating (Integer bounded strictly between 1–5), place_id, user_id.

Amenity
Abstract features, facilities, or services accessible within a property (such as WiFi or parking).

Attributes: name (Unique string index), description.

## 🔗 Logic of Relationships (Significance)
Inheritance (|--): By inheriting from BaseModel, we elegantly guarantee that all business classes follow the exact same identification and audit standard without duplicating code.

User ──> Place (1 to 0..*): A User can own and manage multiple listings, but every Place is structurally tied to one unique Owner for accounting and support safety.

User ──> Review (1 to 0..*): A User can author multiple reviews across the platform; each individual review tracks exactly one single author to prevent anonymous rating manipulation.

Place ── Review (1 to 0..*):* Enforces a Composition relationship. Reviews cannot exist as orphan instances. If a property listing (Place) is removed from the platform, its complete historical review log is destroyed in cascade.

Place <──> Amenity (0..* to 0..*): A property can hold many amenities, and a single amenity can belong to many listings, creating a symmetric Many-to-Many map for robust filter indexing.

# 4. API Interaction Flow
The following sequence diagrams trace exactly how information navigates across presentation controllers, the facade boundary, business entities, and database repositories during runtime execution.

## 👤 1. User Registration Flow
Handles the workflow required to establish and secure a new user account on HBnB.

Code snippet
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client / User
    participant API as Presentation Layer<br>(User API)
    participant Facade as Facade<br>(HBnBFacade)
    participant Model as Business Layer<br>(User Model)
    participant DB as Persistence Layer<br>(UserRepository)

    Client->>API: POST /api/v1/users (user_data)
    activate API
    API->>API: Validate input format<br>(Valid email, secure password)

    API->>Facade: register_user(user_data)
    activate Facade

    Facade->>DB: get_by_email(email)
    activate DB
    DB-->>Facade: Returns User or Null
    deactivate DB

    alt Email already exists in the system
        Facade-->>API: Throw Exception (Email already registered)
        API-->>Client: HTTP 400 Bad Request (Error: Email in use)
    else Email available and valid
        Facade->>Model: Instantiate User(data)
        activate Model
        Model->>Model: Hash Password<br>Generate UUID4 & timestamps
        Model-->>Facade: User Object Created
        deactivate Model

        Facade->>DB: save(user_object)
        activate DB
        DB-->>Facade: Confirm save success
        deactivate DB

        Facade-->>API: Return created user data
        deactivate Facade
        API-->>Client: HTTP 201 Created (ID, Name, Email, etc.)
    end
    deactivate API


## 🏡 2. Place Creation Flow
Executes when an authenticated user attempts to publish a new property listing.

Code snippet
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Host as Host (User)
    participant API as Presentation Layer<br>(Place API)
    participant Facade as Facade<br>(HBnBFacade)
    participant DB_User as Persistence Layer<br>(UserRepository)
    participant Model as Business Layer<br>(Place Model)
    participant DB_Place as Persistence Layer<br>(PlaceRepository)

    Host->>API: POST /api/v1/places (place_data, owner_id)
    activate API

    API->>Facade: create_place(place_data, owner_id)
    activate Facade

    Facade->>DB_User: get_by_id(owner_id)
    activate DB_User
    DB_User-->>Facade: Returns User object (or Null)
    deactivate DB_User

    alt Owner ID does not exist
        Facade-->>API: Throw Exception (User not found)
        API-->>Host: HTTP 404 Not Found (Invalid property owner)
    else Valid User
        Facade->>Model: Instantiate Place(data, owner_id)
        activate Model
        Model->>Model: Validate coordinates & price<br>Generate UUID4
        Model-->>Facade: Place Object Created
        deactivate Model

        Facade->>DB_Place: save(place_object)
        activate DB_Place
        DB_Place-->>Facade: Confirm save success
        deactivate DB_Place

        Facade-->>API: Return created place data
        deactivate Facade
        API-->>Host: HTTP 201 Created (Place Details)
    end
    deactivate API


## ⭐ 3. Review Submission Flow
Triggers when an individual posts experience ratings and comments for a validated listing.

Code snippet
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Guest as Guest (User)
    participant API as Presentation Layer<br>(Review API)
    participant Facade as Facade<br>(HBnBFacade)
    participant DB as Persistence Layer<br>(User/Place Repos)
    participant Model as Business Layer<br>(Review Model)
    participant DB_Rev as Persistence Layer<br>(ReviewRepository)

    Guest->>API: POST /api/v1/places/{place_id}/reviews (comment, rating, user_id)
    activate API

    API->>Facade: add_review(place_id, user_id, comment, rating)
    activate Facade

    Facade->>DB: Verify User and Place existence
    activate DB
    DB-->>Facade: Both exist (Validation Successful)
    deactivate DB

    Facade->>Model: Instantiate Review(comment, rating, place_id, user_id)
    activate Model
    Model->>Model: Validate score range (1 to 5)
    Model-->>Facade: Review Object Ready
    deactivate Model

    Facade->>DB_Rev: save(review_object)
    activate DB_Rev
    DB_Rev-->>Facade: Confirm save success
    deactivate DB_Rev

    Facade-->>API: Return review confirmation
    deactivate Facade
    API-->>Guest: HTTP 201 Created (Review saved successfully)
    deactivate API


## 🔍 4. Fetching a List of Places Flow
Handles the non-transactional query thread when a user evaluates listings based on filtering criteria.

Code snippet
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client / User
    participant API as Presentation Layer<br>(Place API)
    participant Facade as Facade<br>(HBnBFacade)
    participant DB as Persistence Layer<br>(PlaceRepository)

